  "worked_solution": "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x$ is given by\n\n$$\n{0}^{\u2218}\\le \\theta \\le {180}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and second quadrants.\n\nSince $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ is positive, our answer is an angle that lies in the first quadrant, where cosine is positive.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14035417/assets/ca39c4cde40b99fd40a11746a31398d82814268b2df706e3101ee88648c9e2d4.png)\n\nFrom the values in the first quadrant, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({45}^{\u2218})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\narccos\\,(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={45}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
